>> title: Egg Salad
>> category: Salads
>> tags: eggs, mayonnaise, no-cook dressing, sandwich filling, make-ahead
>> counters: Deli
>> aka: deli egg salad, egg mayonnaise, egg salad spread, chopped egg salad
>> pairs-with: mayonnaise, white-sandwich-bread, deli-rye-bread
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 30 min
>> step.1: boil the eggs 11 min, ice them
>> step.2: peel and chop coarse
>> step.3: whisk the dressing
>> step.4: fold, keeping the pieces
>> step.5: chill 1 hr

Boil @eggs{8%large} in @water{2%qt}(enough to cover by an inch) for ~boil{11%min} from a rolling start, then lift them straight into @ice water{1%qt}.

Peel @&(~1)cooled eggs{} under running water and chop them coarse, on a board with a knife.

Whisk @mayonnaise{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @Dijon mustard{2%tsp}, @lemon juice{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{3/4%tsp} and @white pepper{1/4%tsp} together.

Fold @&(~1)dressing{} into @&(~2)chopped eggs{} with @celery{1%rib}(diced fine) and @chives{2%Tbs}(sliced thin), turning it over five or six times and no more.

Chill @&(~1)egg salad{} ~chill{1%hr} so it firms up enough to sit on bread without sliding off.
